<Sigh/>

I really wanted to buck the standard V first ascension trend, but fate
and the RNG seem to have conspired against me.

Anyway... after lots of messing around with W, V, T, M, R, I started
getting a few V and W further and further down in the Dungeons - I was
able to do Sokoban and clear out the Mines fairly regularly.

I think at least one W made it to the castle, but I'm not at all sure.
In any case, my Vs started really racking up the points, a couple
getting into Gehennom proper (checked the score list - no W past DL18,
so they haven't even seen Medusa yet).

One V got all the way down to the sanctum, where she got slimed :(. I
was holding <SPACE> to get past all the ``* hits!'' messages, and so
missed most of the post-death analysis.

At that stage, I was fairly confident that I could get the amulet at
least, and at least get back up to DL1 before dying horribly.

So - Another_Bloody_Valk was born, raised and dumped unceremoniously at
the entrance to some nasty-looking caves by her uncaring parents (They
wanted a boy).

Blah Blah Blah... dead pet... Blah Blah Blah...

First nice thing I remember:

lvlX - co-aligned altar + mines entrance
lvlX+1 - oracle
lvlX+2 - sokoban entrance

This made for some real fun, running back and forth for a while. I think
I did sokoban first("oR), then went down and decimated minetown.

There was a bones file below the town, which gave me some nice toys -
nothing too overpowering at this stage iirc. there was a cursed (oH,
which got blessed ASAP.

At some point though, I found a /oW - SDSM, CoMR, other goodies.

>From then on, it was basically just a slog down to Medusa, who got
chopped with MJ, castle was easy - stand strategically to only let one
or two nasties come at me at once - and down into Gehennom.

VotD was simple - hack, slash, chop.

The mazes got paths dug between < and > as I went - also dug out a nice
path at the edge of the map to make life easier.

None of the Princes gave me any real trouble - MJ makes short work of
the buggers.

Found the tower and wandered up quietly, then went VS hunting - tracked
it down fastly. Rodney fell to a blast from a /oD, and the book was
Mine!!!!

I'd picked up a silver saber a while back, which made the various & much
easier.

The _ command came in very useful - flew down to the square, created the
steps, ran down and started chopping the bad things.

Used the ants to my benefit - step ROUND them, not through - and
focused on clearing away the priests.

Rodney re-appeared only a couple of times, I didn't even bother zapping
him most of the time... grab the amulet, runrunrunrunrunrunrun.

Don't think I got hit by the mysterious force _at_all_, so I FLEW up the
levels and all the way to DL1, where I saved for the night.

Killing some time at work today, with some nice EndGame spoilers open:

Earth - easy, swapping between MJ and my trusty pickaxe made travel
simple.

Air - easy too: I was expecting to struggle with the Elementals more,
but they don't do _that_ much damage, really...

Water - grrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrr. that's a nice surprise, I like the
whole moving landscape thing - could be put to good use elsewhere in the
game methinks.

Fire - boring... it's just kinda slow looking for the right pile of
gold.

Astral - yummy, a pet Angel! went left, centre, right - Cha, Neu, Law
respectively. I could have gone out in style by wishing for a [oOA, but
hell, I might as well do it right the first time...

Riders were easy enough - /oD takes them down fast, #two'ing MJ and a
saber fries them when that misses.

Silly me tried dropping the " and sac'ing it that way.... :p

